{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++ code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nAssume that sk(n) equals the sum of digits of number n in the k-based notation. For example, s2(5)\u2009=\u2009s2(1012)\u2009=\u20091\u2009+\u20090\u2009+\u20091\u2009=\u20092, s3(14)\u2009=\u2009s3(1123)\u2009=\u20091\u2009+\u20091\u2009+\u20092\u2009=\u20094.The sequence of integers a0,\u2009...,\u2009an\u2009-\u20091 is defined as . Your task is to calculate the number of distinct subsequences of sequence a0,\u2009...,\u2009an\u2009-\u20091. Calculate the answer modulo 109\u2009+\u20097.Sequence a1,\u2009...,\u2009ak is called to be a subsequence of sequence b1,\u2009...,\u2009bl, if there is a sequence of indices 1\u2009\u2264\u2009i1\u2009&lt;\u2009...\u2009&lt;\u2009ik\u2009\u2264\u2009l, such that a1\u2009=\u2009bi1, ..., ak\u2009=\u2009bik. In particular, an empty sequence (i.e. the sequence consisting of zero elements) is a subsequence of any sequence.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++ code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cctype>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint readInt() {\n    int x = 0;\n    char c = getchar();\n    while (c <= ' ') c = getchar();\n    bool neg = false;\n    if (c == '-') { neg = true; c = getchar(); }\n    for (; isdigit(c); c = getchar()) x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n    return neg ? -x : x;\n}\n\nvoid printInt(ll x) {\n    if (x < 0) { putchar('-'); x = -x; }\n    if (x > 9) printInt(x / 10);\n    putchar(x % 10 + '0');\n}\n\nint digitSumMod(int x, int K) {\n    int s = 0;\n    while (x) {\n        s += x % K;\n        x /= K;\n    }\n    return s % K;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = readInt(), K = readInt();\n    vector<ll> dp(K, 0);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        int r = digitSumMod(i, K);\n        ll sum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < K; ++j) {\n            if (j != r) sum = (sum + dp[j]) % MOD;\n        }\n        dp[r] = (dp[r] + sum + 1) % MOD;\n    }\n    \n    ll ans = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < K; ++i) ans = (ans + dp[i]) % MOD;\n    \n    printInt(ans);\n    putchar('\\n');\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint readInt() {\n    int x = 0;\n    char c = getchar();\n    while (c <= ' ') c = getchar();\n    bool neg = false;\n    if (c == '-') { neg = true; c = getchar(); }\n    for (; isdigit(c); c = getchar()) x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n    return neg ? -x : x;\n}\n\nvoid printInt(ll x) {\n    if (x < 0) { putchar('-'); x = -x; }\n    if (x > 9) printInt(x / 10);\n    putchar(x % 10 + '0');\n}\n\nint digitSumMod(int x, int K) {\n    int s = 0;\n    while (x) {\n        s += x % K;\n        x /= K;\n    }\n    return s % K;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n = readInt(), K = readInt();\n    vector<ll> dp(K, 0);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        int r = digitSumMod(i, K);\n        ll sum = 0;\n  